      "solution": "n = int(input())\ndp = [1e9] * 1005\n\nfor i in range(1,1005):\n    if str(i).count('1') == len(str(i)):\n        dp[i] = len(str(i))\n    for j in range(1,i):\n        dp[i] = min(dp[i], dp[j] + dp[i-j])\n    for j in range(1,i):\n        if i%j == 0:\n            dp[i] = min(dp[i], dp[j] + dp[i//j])\n    \nprint(dp[n])\n",
      "statement": "You are given an integer [[n]]. You have to represent the number [[n]] with a mathematical notation consisting of only these symbols: {{1}}, {{+}}, {{×}}, {{(}}, and {{)}}, where the only valid arithmetic operations are addition and multiplication. Numbers such as {{11}} or {{111}} are allowed. Find the minimum number of {{1}}s required to represent [[n]].\n\nFor example, the number 14 can be represented by {{11 + (1 + 1) + 1}}, or {{(1 + 1) × (1 + (1 + 1 + 1) × (1 + 1))}}. So for 14, the answer would be 5.",
